    # ── String operation workloads with pre-built fixtures ────────────────────
    # Fixtures are embedded as string LITERALS in each generated program.
    # No runtime concat/repeat — the timed code measures only the operation.
    # Source and delimiter are hoisted out of the loop, so we measure the op,
    # not literal allocation per iteration.

    # F1: split short Inline fixture → 6 inline segments. Tests Inline path.
    "split short literal 100k": {
